  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef rl_q_learning_update(q_values: list, state: int, action: int, reward: float, next_state: int, done: int, lr: float = 0.1, gamma: float = 0.99) -> list:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Q-Learning Update** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef rl_q_learning_update(q_values: list, state: int, action: int, reward: float, next_state: int, done: int, lr: float = 0.1, gamma: float = 0.99) -> list:\n    Q = np.array(q_values, dtype=np.float64)\n    mx = np.max(Q[int(next_state)]) if done == 0 else 0.0\n    Q[int(state), int(action)] += float(lr) * (float(reward) + float(gamma)*mx - Q[int(state), int(action)])\n    return np.round(Q, 6).tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
